---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Every week pairs a lecture on one predictive-text domain with a lab where
    you build or interrogate an artefact from it: a toy T9 disambiguator, an
    autocorrect you deliberately break, an audit of your own inbox's smart
    replies, a side-by-side of three forecast UIs and how each one hides its
    uncertainty. You leave the semester with a small portfolio of builds and
    case studies, and a final project that turns one of them into a proper
    audit of a real product's suggestion design.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    A student a couple of years into a CS or HCI-adjacent degree who already
    writes small programs without help, and who is more interested in why a
    piece of software suggests what it suggests than in shipping a polished
    app. If you have never once been annoyed at autocorrect, or "it's just
    next-token prediction" feels like it ends the conversation rather than
    starting one, this course is aimed a little past you.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The twelve-week schedule and what to bring to each lab.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Policies" href="/policies/">
      <p>Late work, extensions, and how you're allowed to use predictive tools here.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
